# Stable device identity for the CS7.1 classifier camera.
#
# Matches on USB vendor ID and product ID - not the serial number as well,
# unlike 99-cs71.rules for the controller adapter. That rule needs a serial
# number because "any generic USB-serial adapter" is a broad class it must
# not accidentally match; this rule matches a specific camera module already
# chosen for this appliance (3DModels/Classifier/CameraV2), where exactly one
# unit is expected to ever be attached, and many inexpensive UVC modules do
# not reliably program a unique USB serial string in the first place. No
# camera has been approved with recorded hardware evidence yet; the two
# placeholders below are substituted by install.sh, the same way the
# controller adapter's are. This file as checked in matches nothing until
# that substitution happens.
#
# TAG+="systemd" plus SYSTEMD_WANTS starts cs71-vision.service the moment the
# camera is present, the same reason 99-cs71.rules does it for cs71d.service.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTRS{idVendor}=="@@CAMERA_VENDOR_ID@@", ATTRS{idProduct}=="@@CAMERA_PRODUCT_ID@@", SYMLINK+="cs71vision", GROUP="cs71-vision", MODE="0660", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="cs71-vision.service"
